# Complete End-to-End Pipelines for Aqua-Predict-NB

This document details the architecture and implementation plan for building the complete production-grade pipelines for **Aqua-Predict-NB** (AI Groundwater Level Forecasting for New Brunswick Private Wells), translating the research proposal and architecture into fully functioning Python and web pipelines.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **PyTorch Installation**: PyTorch will be installed in your Python 3.14 environment via `pip install torch`.
> 
> **Data Generation & Ingestion Strategy**: Real New Brunswick Online Well Log System (OWLS) and ECCC climate stations span key New Brunswick hydrogeological regions (Fredericton, Moncton, Saint John, Miramichi, Bathurst, Edmundston, Sussex, etc.). The ingestion pipeline will implement realistic NB multi-basin data generation adhering strictly to the provincial hydrogeology (fractured bedrock, Carboniferous sandstones, Quaternary glaciofluvial, Windsor group karst, with geochemical risk overlays for Arsenic, Uranium, and Methane), alongside real ECCC climate station coordinates and meteorological characteristics.

---

## Architecture Overview

```
Aqua-Predict-NB Pipeline Architecture:
├── Raw Data Ingestion (NB OWLS format + ECCC Climate Stations + NB Geological Survey)
│     ├── Well construction: static water level, total depth, casing depth, lithology
│     ├── Climate drivers: daily & monthly precipitation, temperature (mean/max/min), snowpack
│     └── Geochemical overlays: Arsenic (mafic/slate), Uranium (granites), Methane (Carboniferous)
│
├── Feature Engineering & Hydrogeological Preprocessing
│     ├── Rolling meteorological lag features (30d, 90d, 180d, 365d cumulative precipitation)
│     ├── Standardized Precipitation Evapotranspiration (SPEI/SPI proxy) & Snowmelt recharge
│     ├── Cyclical seasonal features (sin/cos of month and day of year)
│     ├── Static well & geological embeddings (depth ratio, aquifer type, spatial coordinates)
│     └── Sequence windowing (24-month lookback -> 6-month multi-step forecast)
│
├── PyTorch LSTM Model & Bayesian Uncertainty (MCDO)
│     ├── Multivariate Seq2Seq LSTM with static covariate fusion
│     ├── Monte Carlo Dropout (N=100 stochastic forward passes at inference)
│     ├── Quantile / Pinball loss + MSE dual-objective training
│     └── Hydrogeological validation metrics (NSE, KGE, RMSE, MAE, PICP, MPIW)
│
├── Risk Tiering & Multimodal Hazard Assessment
│     ├── Drought risk classification (<10th %ile = High, 10-25th = Medium, >25th = Low)
│     └── Joint Drought + Geochemical risk indexing (Arsenic, Uranium, Methane concentration risk)
│
├── Export & Visualizations Pipeline
│     ├── High-resolution scientific figures & publication charts (`outputs/figures/`)
│     ├── Automated serialization to GeoJSON / JSON (`data/processed_wells.json`)
│     ├── Dynamic dashboard loading in `script.js` with live metrics sync
│     └── Standalone CLI runner (`run_pipeline.py`) supporting modular stages
│
└── Test Suite
      └── Automated pytest / unittest coverage for data, models, inference, and pipeline orchestration
```

