### 2. Core Python Pipeline Package (`src/`)

#### [NEW] [src/config.py](file:///c:/Users/delef/.gemini/antigravity/Aqua-Predict-NB/src/config.py)
- Configuration dataclasses and constants:
  - Filepaths: raw data, processed features, checkpoints, figure outputs, exported artifacts.
  - Hydrogeological parameters: NB spatial bounds ($44.5^\circ-48.2^\circ$N, $-69.1^\circ--63.7^\circ$W), aquifer categories, geochemical risk thresholds.
  - Model hyperparameters: `lookback_months=24`, `forecast_horizon=6`, `hidden_dim=128`, `num_layers=2`, `dropout=0.2`, `mc_samples=100`, `learning_rate=1e-3`, `batch_size=64`, `epochs=30`.

#### [NEW] [src/data/ingestion.py](file:///c:/Users/delef/.gemini/antigravity/Aqua-Predict-NB/src/data/ingestion.py)
- Ingestion engine for NB OWLS wells, ECCC climate records, and geological atlas:
  - Generates/processes province-wide well records covering New Brunswick counties (York, Westmorland, Saint John, Northumberland, Gloucester, Madawaska, Kings, Carleton, etc.).
  - Simulates/downloads multi-year monthly meteorological series for ECCC reference stations (Fredericton CDA, Moncton Airport, Saint John A, Bathurst A, Miramichi, St. Leonard).
  - Assigns hydrogeological formations and geochemical threat indicators based on New Brunswick bedrock geology.

#### [NEW] [src/data/preprocessing.py](file:///c:/Users/delef/.gemini/antigravity/Aqua-Predict-NB/src/data/preprocessing.py)
- Feature engineering engine:
  - Time series alignment between climate stations and nearest well locations (spatial KDTree/distance weighting).
  - Rolling precipitation accumulations (30-day, 90-day, 180-day, 365-day) capturing shallow vs. deep bedrock lag responses.
  - Cyclical harmonic temporal encoding ($\sin(2\pi m / 12), \cos(2\pi m / 12)$).
  - Standardization and normalization with serializable scalers.

#### [NEW] [src/data/dataset.py](file:///c:/Users/delef/.gemini/antigravity/Aqua-Predict-NB/src/data/dataset.py)
- PyTorch `Dataset` and `DataLoader` classes:
  - Windowing function slicing 24-month input sequences and 6-month target sequences.
  - Batched static well metadata integration (well depth, casing depth, aquifer type one-hot).

#### [NEW] [src/models/lstm_forecaster.py](file:///c:/Users/delef/.gemini/antigravity/Aqua-Predict-NB/src/models/lstm_forecaster.py)
- PyTorch LSTM neural network:
  - Dynamic sequence encoder (2-layer LSTM, 128 hidden units, dropout 0.2).
  - Static covariate fusion layer (combines static geological/construction features with LSTM latent state).
  - Multi-step forecasting head predicting 6 months ahead.
  - Monte Carlo Dropout wrapper enabling uncertainty bounds estimation at inference time without needing retraining.

#### [NEW] [src/models/train.py](file:///c:/Users/delef/.gemini/antigravity/Aqua-Predict-NB/src/models/train.py)
- Complete training loop:
  - Loss functions: MSE + Pinball / Quantile loss for calibration.
  - Optimizer: AdamW with weight decay and gradient clipping.
  - Learning rate scheduler: ReduceLROnPlateau.
  - Early stopping and model checkpoint saving (`checkpoints/best_model.pt`).

#### [NEW] [src/models/evaluate.py](file:///c:/Users/delef/.gemini/antigravity/Aqua-Predict-NB/src/models/evaluate.py)
- Evaluation and hydrogeological benchmarking:
  - Nash-Sutcliffe Efficiency (NSE) — standard gold standard in hydrological forecasting.
  - Kling-Gupta Efficiency (KGE).
  - Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE) and Mean Absolute Error (MAE).
  - Prediction Interval Coverage Probability (PICP) and Mean Prediction Interval Width (MPIW) for $P_{10}-P_{90}$ intervals.

#### [NEW] [src/inference/predict.py](file:///c:/Users/delef/.gemini/antigravity/Aqua-Predict-NB/src/inference/predict.py)
- Full inference pipeline:
  - Runs Monte Carlo Dropout ($N=100$) over test wells to generate median ($P_{50}$), conservative high-risk ($P_{10}$), and optimistic low-risk ($P_{90}$) groundwater level projections.

#### [NEW] [src/inference/risk_tiering.py](file:///c:/Users/delef/.gemini/antigravity/Aqua-Predict-NB/src/inference/risk_tiering.py)
- Hydrogeological risk classifier:
  - Evaluates forecast depth against well-specific historical percentiles:
    - High Risk: Forecast level $< 10\text{th}$ percentile of historical record (imminent pump intake breach).
    - Medium Risk: Forecast level between $10\text{th}$ and $25\text{th}$ percentile.
    - Low Risk: Forecast level $> 25\text{th}$ percentile.
  - Calculates combined drought + water quality risk index (flagging wells where water table drop concentrates Arsenic, Uranium, or Methane).

#### [NEW] [src/export/export_figures.py](file:///c:/Users/delef/.gemini/antigravity/Aqua-Predict-NB/src/export/export_figures.py)
- Dedicated Matplotlib/Seaborn visualization pipeline generating all 5 publication-ready PNG/SVG figures:
  - Forecast hydrographs with Monte Carlo Dropout uncertainty bands.
  - Spatial New Brunswick risk map with geochemical overlays.
  - Loss & convergence curves.
  - Lag correlation matrix.
  - Drought risk distribution summary.

#### [NEW] [src/export/export_dashboard.py](file:///c:/Users/delef/.gemini/antigravity/Aqua-Predict-NB/src/export/export_dashboard.py)
- Exporter module generating:
  - `data/processed_wells.json`: Contains real NB well coordinates, construction depths, aquifer types, geochemical flags, baseline levels, and LSTM 6-month forecasted trajectories ($P_{10}, P_{50}, P_{90}$).
  - `data/pipeline_summary.json`: Province-wide summary statistics (total monitored wells, count in high drought risk, count in combined geo-risk, overall model RMSE, NSE).

